---
import { Counter } from 'pre.style-demo-react-ui';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Interpolation">
  <h1>Interpolation</h1>
  <p>
    These counts are set with <code>{'${…}'}</code> in a block, and shown by its
    <code>&amp;::before</code>. Each value becomes a generated class that sets a custom property,
    using pre.style's small runtime. Blocks without <code>{'${…}'}</code> don't use it.
  </p>
  <h2>In a client script</h2>
  <p id="count"></p>
  <h2>In a React island</h2>
  <Counter client:load />
  <p>
    A frontmatter or template block can't use <code>{'${…}'}</code>: that code only runs on the
    server, so nothing could set the value in the browser. Each new value adds a rule that's never
    removed, so for values that change this often, a real app would use <code>style</code> instead.
  </p>
</Layout>

<script>
  import { css } from '@pre.style/core';

  const element = document.getElementById('count')!;
  let i = 0;

  // Astro bundles this script for the browser, so it can use runtime values.
  (function inc() {
    element.className = css`
      font-size: 3rem;
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
      font-weight: 700;
      margin: 0;

      &::before {
        content: var(${JSON.stringify(String(i))}, '0');
      }
    `;
    i++;
    setTimeout(inc, 1000);
  })();
</script>
